WEBVTT

00:03.920 --> 00:05.720
Okay, so now what is exactly right?

00:05.760 --> 00:06.160
Join.

00:06.160 --> 00:08.520
This is the total opposite of the left join.

00:08.520 --> 00:14.880
So this type of returns all the rows from the right table and only the matching from the left table.

00:14.880 --> 00:17.960
So here the main table the main focus is the right table.

00:17.960 --> 00:22.960
So SQL gonna get you all the rows everything from the table B the right table.

00:22.960 --> 00:26.280
But from the left side we will get only the matching data.

00:26.280 --> 00:31.720
So that means in the left side you will get only the data that has a match on the right side.

00:31.720 --> 00:36.480
And with that the right table can be the primary, the main source of your data.

00:36.480 --> 00:37.920
So it is very important table.

00:37.920 --> 00:39.960
But the left table is not that important.

00:39.960 --> 00:43.560
You are just joining it in order to get additional data.

00:43.560 --> 00:46.080
So again about the syntax it's not that crazy.

00:46.120 --> 00:48.800
All what you have to do is to change the join type.

00:48.800 --> 00:51.200
So instead of left you say right join.

00:51.200 --> 00:56.720
And again here the order of the tables is very important because the side here makes a difference.

00:56.720 --> 01:01.020
So we start from the left table A and then right join it to the table.

01:01.060 --> 01:03.340
B so it sounds very similar to the left join.

01:03.340 --> 01:04.780
We are just switching things.

01:04.820 --> 01:06.900
Now let's go back to SQL in order to practice.

01:06.940 --> 01:07.580
Okay my friends.

01:07.580 --> 01:08.780
So now we have the following task.

01:08.820 --> 01:16.260
And it says get all customers along with their orders including orders without matching customers.

01:16.300 --> 01:19.740
So again we have the customers and the orders and we are doing the join.

01:19.740 --> 01:21.460
But here the condition is different.

01:21.460 --> 01:25.860
We want to see all the orders even if they don't have a matching customer.

01:25.900 --> 01:31.340
So that means I would like to see everything from the table orders and the customers table here is only

01:31.340 --> 01:33.020
like supporting and helping.

01:33.020 --> 01:36.380
So the main table that we are focusing on is in the orders.

01:36.420 --> 01:39.820
We want to see everything and from the customers only the matching.

01:39.820 --> 01:44.900
And if you are looking currently to the results, you can see we are seeing only three orders, right.

01:44.900 --> 01:50.140
But in the original table, if you go back over here, you can see that we have four orders.

01:50.140 --> 01:54.220
So we are currently using this query not seeing all the orders.

01:54.220 --> 01:55.500
So now how are we going to solve it.

01:55.540 --> 01:58.640
If you start from the table customers you can say you know what?

01:58.680 --> 02:01.880
Instead of left join, we're going to say right join.

02:01.880 --> 02:06.240
And with that, you're going to guarantee you will get everything from the table orders.

02:06.240 --> 02:09.520
But now the left table the customers is not that important.

02:09.520 --> 02:12.680
And you will see the data of the customers only if there is a match.

02:12.680 --> 02:17.920
So doing the right join like this guaranteed to see everything whether there is match or no match.

02:17.920 --> 02:22.480
Now if you go and execute it, you can see on the right side the order ID and the sales.

02:22.480 --> 02:27.160
And we can see now all the orders and on the left side the ID and the first name.

02:27.160 --> 02:30.440
We are seeing only the customers if they did order something.

02:30.440 --> 02:34.200
And for the orders without a known customer we are getting nulls.

02:34.200 --> 02:36.800
So with us we have solved the task using the right join.

02:36.800 --> 02:41.040
So now my friends, you have to go and solve this task to get the exact same results.

02:41.040 --> 02:46.040
But you are allowed to use only the left join, so you are not allowed to use the right join.

02:46.040 --> 02:49.640
So now go pause the video, solve the task and meet you soon.

02:54.960 --> 02:59.100
Now my friends in SQL there is always alternatives on how to solve a task.

02:59.100 --> 03:03.820
So now if you want to get all the data from B and only the matching from A, you can do it like we have

03:03.820 --> 03:05.500
done using the right join.

03:05.500 --> 03:11.620
But if you go and switch the sides and you make the table B as a left table and the table A as the right

03:11.660 --> 03:15.620
table, you can do that, of course, in SQL, but you have to switch the join type.

03:15.620 --> 03:17.980
So instead of right we have to use left.

03:18.020 --> 03:20.980
Now since the B table now on the left side.

03:20.980 --> 03:22.940
And as well you have to switch the order.

03:22.940 --> 03:27.940
So you start from the b table and then you say left join the A table.

03:27.980 --> 03:29.780
And of course the same join condition.

03:29.780 --> 03:33.860
And if you do that you will get the exact same result as the left query.

03:33.860 --> 03:39.700
So if you just switch the tables and as well switch the join type, you can get the same results.

03:39.700 --> 03:42.620
And to be honest my friends, I don't like the right join.

03:42.660 --> 03:47.860
It's just in the last ten years, I always tend to start from a table and then use a left join.

03:47.860 --> 03:52.380
And from my point of view, the left join is way more famous than the right join.

03:52.380 --> 03:55.940
And I think I never used a query where I'm using a right join.

03:56.040 --> 04:00.520
So my advice for you always try to skip the right join and stick with the left join.

04:00.520 --> 04:04.600
Just get the order of the tables in the query correct and you will get the same results.

04:04.600 --> 04:07.080
So with that you know an alternative for the right join.

04:07.120 --> 04:10.440
Now all that you have to do is to go and switch the right to left.

04:10.480 --> 04:13.360
And this is not enough because if I go and execute it.

04:13.400 --> 04:17.200
So now all what I have to do is to go and switch the tables like this.

04:17.480 --> 04:22.680
So we start from the table orders, because I want to see everything from the orders and then left,

04:22.680 --> 04:24.320
join it with the customers.

04:24.360 --> 04:26.280
And of course we don't have to change anything here.

04:26.280 --> 04:29.880
It doesn't matter the order because we have an equal operator here.

04:29.880 --> 04:35.600
What is very important here is where you start from which table and what is the table that you are joining

04:35.600 --> 04:36.000
with.

04:36.000 --> 04:39.840
So if you go and execute it, you will get the exact same results.

04:39.840 --> 04:41.680
So now I'm seeing all the orders.

04:41.680 --> 04:45.120
I'm not missing anything and only the matching customers.

04:45.120 --> 04:48.920
And I prefer this way solving this task instead of using the right join.

04:48.960 --> 04:49.320
All right.

04:49.320 --> 04:50.960
So that's all about the right join.

04:51.000 --> 04:52.720
Next we're going to combine everything.

04:52.720 --> 04:54.880
We're going to talk about the full join.

04:54.880 --> 04:55.600
So let's go.
